# PERC-equivalent coverage report — open-source aggregate
# (ORGANIC-20260601 v2.3 Step 28 PERC / 'last commercial gate').
# Calibre PERC = Programmable Electrical Rule Check (ties layout to
# circuit). Commercial Calibre PERC was NOT run. This aggregates the
# open-source equivalents for the 7 PERC categories.
#
# Status legend: AUTOMATED = tool-proven | GUARDBAND = design rule |
#   MANUAL_REVIEW = needs human sign-off | N/A = does not apply.
#
OVERALL VERDICT: PERC_EQUIV_INCOMPLETE
Commercial Calibre PERC run: NO (open-source equivalent)

# === Per-category status ===
  [AUTOMATED    ] PASS           Antenna
       tool: OpenROAD check_antennas  (tool verdict: PASS)
       
  [AUTOMATED    ] PASS           IR drop
       tool: OpenROAD PSM analyze_power_grid  (tool verdict: PASS)
       
  [AUTOMATED    ] INCOMPLETE     EM (electromigration)
       tool: OpenROAD PSM analyze_power_grid -enable_em  (tool verdict: MEASURED)
       measurement-only artifact (no budget comparison applied) — review required (#444)
  [AUTOMATED    ] REVIEW         Floating nets
       tool: OpenROAD report_floating_nets (ERC screen)  (tool verdict: BENIGN-ERC)
       benign float verdict from the #696 ERC screen (VPWR/VGND/zero_/spare structural floats) — non-blocking review item, not a conclusive PERC defect (#698)
  [GUARDBAND    ] GUARDBAND      EM current-density / via-array guardband
       tool: design-rule (guardband)
       stated as a GUARDBAND, NOT a commercial-tool EM sign-off; verify against the PDK Jmax tables at the target lifetime.
  [N/A          ] N/A            ESD protection presence
       tool: DEF/GDS pad-ring scan (presence) + MANUAL confirm
       N/A (no pad ring — core macro). ESD protection is the top-level pad frame's responsibility; a core-only macro has no chip pads to protect. (0 structural ring filler(s) seen.)
  [AUTOMATED    ] PASS           Latch-up well-tap presence
       tool: DEF COMPONENTS well/substrate-tap scan (open-source PERC-equiv)
       9358 well/substrate-tap cell(s) present. NECESSARY-BUT-NOT-SUFFICIENT: proves taps were inserted, but does NOT prove tap SPACING (max-tap-distance — DRC deck) nor the device-physics latch-up criterion (Vhold>Vdd, SCR beta product, guard-ring efficacy) — those stay MANUAL.
  [MANUAL_REVIEW] MANUAL_REVIEW  Latch-up / well-tap (spacing + device-physics)
       tool: Magic DRC well-tap rules (rides existing DRC deck) + MANUAL
       tap PRESENCE is automated above; tap SPACING (max-tap-distance) is screened by the Magic/KLayout DRC deck; full latch-up sign-off (holding voltage Vhold>Vdd, parasitic-SCR beta product, guard-ring efficacy under injected substrate current) needs commercial PERC + manual confirm — device physics, not derivable from DEF.
  [N/A          ] N/A            Cross-voltage-domain
       tool: DEF NETS+SPECIALNETS power-domain count + level-shifter cell scan
       single supply (1 power / 1 ground domain family, via USE-keyword) — no cross-voltage-domain crossings possible.
  [SEMI_AUTOMATED] REVIEW         Latch-up tap spacing (geometry)
       tool: DEF tap/std-cell placement coverage screen (open-source)
       every one of 804 placed std cell(s) is within the conservative 30.0 um screening radius of a rated tap. NECESSARY-BUT-NOT-SUFFICIENT: this screens coverage at a pitch LOOSER than (and therefore cannot certify) the real foundry max-tap-distance rule, and proves NOTHING about the device-physics latch-up criterion (Vhold>Vdd, parasitic-SCR beta product, guard-ring efficacy). NOT an automated latch-up PASS.
  [SEMI_AUTOMATED] NA             Guard-ring topology (geometry)
       tool: DEF guard-ring master + IO/high-current proximity screen
       No guard-ring cells AND no IO / high-current cells placed — a low-current digital core; core guard rings are not expected (latch-up robustness rests on tap density, screened separately).

